From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anirudh Srinivasan <asrinivasan@oss.tenstorrent.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:52:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] riscv: Add Spacemit K3 machine

Add a spacemit-k3 machine based on the RVA23 compliant Spacemit K3
SoC[1]. This machine currently models the single boot hart (Spacemit
X100) in the system, a uart, boot media (SPI NOR, SD, EMMC, UFS) and
boot-mode selection. This machine accepts the bootrom dumped from the
hardware via -bios, which loads the next boot stage from boot media
based on the boot-mode selection.

[1] https://github.com/spacemit-com/docs-chip/blob/main/en/key_stone/k3/k3_docs/k3_ds.md

Signed-off-by: Anirudh Srinivasan <asrinivasan@oss.tenstorrent.com>

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/qemu-riscv/20261124-spacemit_k3-v1-5-e911d6e88542@oss.tenstorrent.com/]

[tgamblin: taken from the v2 work in progress at
 https://github.com/asrinivasanTT/qemu/commit/dcdc21d1a424728c5f76738e54810338192a503a]
[tgamblin: backport to QEMU 11.1.3: drop the MemoryRegion argument from
 the riscv_{imsic,aplic,aclint_mtimer,aclint_swi}_create() calls, which
 11.1.3 does not have (they always use system memory), and register the
 machine with riscv64_machine_interfaces so that it is listed in
 qemu-system-riscv64]
Signed-off-by: Trevor Gamblin <tgamblin@baylibre.com>
